# Finance 11: Several assets

A `Field` prices options on one asset. Real books hold options on many, each with its own market, its own model and often its own engine. A `module::Chord` coordinates several `Field`s: each asset keeps every property of a `Field`, and the `Chord` adds the names, one `price` call across all of them, and the batching that makes pricing many assets cost little more than pricing one. After this chapter you can build a `Chord`, price assets with different models together, read each asset's result by name, see which assets were merged into one call, and take the implied-volatility smile of all of them.

Every program is complete and its output is the output of that program.

## The mental model

- **A `Chord` is a collection of `Field`s, not a bigger `Field`.** A `Field` stays one asset on one continuous process, so its methods are unambiguous; the `Chord` adds only what is about several.
- **Every operation is the `Field`'s own operation, applied to each asset.** Each asset keeps its model and engine, and the result for an asset equals pricing it alone.
- **The calls run concurrently.** What cannot be merged is priced on several threads at once, with identical numbers.
- **Assets that can share a call are merged.** Same engine, controls and model family, with European exercise (Black-Scholes on the analytic engine and Heston and Bates on the COS engine even with different parameters; the FFT needs equal parameters): their strips are priced once and split back.

| Entry point | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `Chord{{name, field}, ...}`, `Chord::add`, `at`, `contains` | build the collection from a dictionary of assets and reach an asset |
| `Chord::from_model_params` | build a Chord of assets of any model from a table of model parameters |
| `Chord::price` | price every asset, returning a `Chord::Result` |
| `Chord::implied_vol` | the implied volatilities of every asset's own prices |
| `Chord::batches`, `validate` | how many calls a price makes; check every asset at once |
| `Chord::simulate_paths`, `price_corr`, `var_corr` | correlated paths of all assets, whatever their model (Black-Scholes, Heston, Bates, SABR), for baskets and spreads |

